    "title": "pandas.Index.argsort — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.argsort#\n\n- \nIndex.argsort(**args* ,***kwargs* )[source]#\n- Return the integer indices that would sort the index. \n  - Parameters\n    - ***args**\n    - Passed to numpy.ndarray.argsort.\n    - ****kwargs**\n    - Passed to numpy.ndarray.argsort.\n  - Returns\n    - np.ndarray[np.intp]\n    - Integer indices that would sort the index if used as an indexer.\n See also \n  - `numpy.argsort`\n  - Similar method for NumPy arrays.\n  - `Index.sort_values`\n  - Return sorted copy of Index.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.Index(['b', 'a', 'd', 'c']) >>> idx Index(['b', 'a', 'd', 'c'], dtype='object') >>> order = idx.argsort() >>> order array([1, 0, 3, 2]) >>> idx[order] Index(['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'], dtype='object')",
